       "Stone round: the stone travels hand to hand round the circle in order, low, two hands to two hands. Each holder may add ONE small true thing — something from the story retold in their own words, something true about this place ('the river is near our park'), or simply the people's name said carefully, which counts in full and is honoured at full size: a name said right by a three-year-old is this record's whole curriculum arriving. A holder who only wants to hold the stone and pass it on has also taken a complete turn.",
