      ["big spring leaves, adult-gathered (the largest soft green leaves of the season — sycamore, big maple, hosta-sized garden leaves; gathered fresh, rinsed, checked: no thorns, no brittle edges, nothing from a sprayed bed)", "a sunny spot the adult has chosen in advance (the light window — somewhere the group can stand with the sun in front of them and shade behind)", "a small basket the leaves retire to (the leaf library)"],
