      safety="Tissues are this record's whole material and they are treated with the plain respect big light things deserve: one tissue in the air at a time, dropped from a standing position at the snowfield's edge — nobody climbs anything to drop from higher, ever, and the want for height is answered with the high box and the adult's own raised hand for the smallest droppers. Watchers stay seated while snow is in the air so that no watcher crosses under a drop or reaches into another's fall; retrievals happen after landing, at walking pace, one person moving. Tissues that have floored are retired to the bank after a few flights rather than flown ragged, and any tissue that reaches a mouth is retired on the spot, without comment or lecture.",
