      ["a wide shallow tub of water, filled to hand-depth (the dipping sea — big enough that a big object enters without splashing the rim)", "big test objects, adult-built and adult-tested (things honestly bigger than a palm whose answer is certain: a wooden block, a smooth stone, a big sponge, a cork the size of a small fist, an empty sealed tub with its lid taped, a big leaf — every one dipped by the adult in advance, because this record never schedules a surprise the adult hasn't met)", "a towel under the tub and a second towel for hands (the shore)"],
