      safety="The bridge is only as honest as its cushions: every cushion passes the adult's full-weight centre-and-edge test before the session, cushions sit butted on a flat rug over a hard floor (never on another mat that can skate), and a cushion that shifts under a crossing foot is re-seated by the adult before the next crosser, without exception or hurry. One crosser on the bridge at a time, always; the adult walks beside every crossing at a distance that can become a catch, and the offered hand is open and still — never gripping, pulling, or steering a crosser by it. Stepping off is designed for, not failed at: the rug makes every step-off a soft arrival, and no crosser is ever lifted back onto the bridge mid-crossing — feet leave the bridge only onto the rug, by the crosser's own step. Running and jumping on the bridge end a crossing kindly and at once, and the bridge waits for walking feet.",
